@Joffcom Actually, the HTTP module gets the correct data but the problem occurs when trying to read an input data that contains offending field name with `$input.all()` (e.g. in the `Code` node) - however, reading an input data with `$json` (e.g. in the `Edit fields (Set)` node) seems to be working fine.

Using the `Code` node (notice the absence of the value in the output):
<img width="1919" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-09 at 14 40 44" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8b089e93-ea5a-48f5-be71-66827fced065" />

JavaScript from the node:
```
return $input.all().map((item) => {
  return {
    key: item.json.key,
    changelog: item.json.changelog.histories.reduce((acc, cur) => {
      cur.items.forEach((item) => {
        if (item.field === 'status') {
          acc.push({
            created_at: cur.created,
            from_status: {
              id: parseInt(item.from),
              name: item.fromString
            },
            to_status: {
              id: parseInt(item.to),
              name: item.toString
            }
          });
        }
      });
  
      return acc;
    }, [])
  }
});
```

Using the `Edit fields (Set)` node (notice the value is there in the output):
<img width="1906" alt="Screenshot 2025-01-09 at 14 42 23" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e358d20f-bfe6-4039-8d37-3bc54081e159" />

JSON from the node:
```
{
  "key": "{{ $json.key }}",
  "changelog": {{ $json.changelog.histories.reduce((acc, cur) => {
    cur.items.forEach((item) => {
      if (item.field === 'status') {
        acc.push({
          createdAt: cur.created,
          fromStatus: {
            id: parseInt(item.from),
            name: item.fromString
          },
          toStatus: {
            id: parseInt(item.to),
            name: item.toString
          }
        });
      }
    });

    return acc;
  }, []) }}
}
```

Let me know if this helps.
